# STREAMLINED WORKFLOW FOR LEVEL 1 TASKS

> **TL;DR:** This document outlines a streamlined workflow for Level 1 (Quick Bug Fix) tasks, focusing on efficient problem resolution with minimal overhead while maintaining adequate documentation.

## Notion backend (this repository)

Memory Bank **storage** is **Notion**: **Task page body**, **Active Context** subpage (`activeContextPageUrl`), **Progress** subpage (`progressPageUrl`) per **`Core/memory-bank-paths.mdc`**. **Active Context:** keep updates **short**; follow **`## Active Context: Notion policy and multi-task`**.

## 🔍 LEVEL 1 WORKFLOW OVERVIEW

Command sequence (same as `README.md`): **`/van` → `/build` → `/reflect` → `/archive`**.

```mermaid
graph LR
    Init["1. INITIALIZATION<br>/van"] --> Impl["2. IMPLEMENTATION<br>/build"]
    Impl --> Reflect["3. REFLECTION<br>/reflect"]
    Reflect --> Archive["4. ARCHIVE<br>/archive"]
    
    Init -.-> InitDocs["Quick setup<br>Issue understanding"]
    Impl -.-> ImplDocs["Focused fix<br>Verify resolution"]
    Reflect -.-> ReflectDocs["Lessons learned<br>brief review"]
    Archive -.-> ArchiveDocs["Completion record<br>handoff"]
```

## 📋 WORKFLOW PHASES

### Phase 1: INITIALIZATION (`/van`)

```mermaid
graph TD
    Start["Start Level 1 Task"] --> Identify["Identify<br>Issue"]
    Identify --> Understand["Understand<br>Problem"]
    Understand --> Setup["Quick<br>Environment Setup"]
    Setup --> TaskEntry["Create Quick<br>Task Entry"]
    TaskEntry --> InitComplete["Initialization<br>Complete"]
```

**Steps:**
1. Identify the specific issue to fix
2. Understand the problem and its impact
3. Set up environment for quick fix
4. Create minimal task entry on the **Task page body** (resolved `taskPageUrl`)

**Milestone Checkpoint:**
```
✓ INITIALIZATION CHECKPOINT
- Issue clearly identified? [YES/NO]
- Problem understood? [YES/NO]
- Environment set up? [YES/NO]
- Task entry created? [YES/NO]

→ If all YES: Proceed to Implementation
→ If any NO: Complete initialization steps
```

### Phase 2: IMPLEMENTATION (`/build`)

```mermaid
graph TD
    Start["Begin<br>Implementation"] --> Locate["Locate<br>Issue Source"]
    Locate --> Develop["Develop<br>Fix"]
    Develop --> Test["Test<br>Solution"]
    Test --> Verify["Verify<br>Resolution"]
    Verify --> ImplComplete["Implementation<br>Complete"]
```

**Steps:**
1. Locate the source of the issue
2. Develop a targeted fix
3. Test the solution thoroughly
4. Verify that the issue is resolved

**Milestone Checkpoint:**
```
✓ IMPLEMENTATION CHECKPOINT
- Issue source located? [YES/NO]
- Fix developed? [YES/NO]
- Solution tested? [YES/NO]
- Resolution verified? [YES/NO]

→ If all YES: Proceed to Reflection
→ If any NO: Complete implementation steps
```

### Phase 3: REFLECTION (`/reflect`)

```mermaid
graph TD
    Start["Begin<br>Reflection"] --> Review["Review fix<br>and process"]
    Review --> Lessons["Capture lessons<br>learned"]
    Lessons --> Persist["Write Reflection<br>artifact"]
    Persist --> ReflectComplete["Reflection<br>Complete"]
```

**Steps:**
1. Review what changed and whether the fix matches the issue
2. Capture brief lessons learned (what worked, risks, follow-ups)
3. Persist the structured reflection on the **Reflection** subpage (`reflectionPageUrl`) per **`Core/memory-bank-paths.mdc`**; file-based: `memory-bank/reflection/reflection-[task_id].md`
4. Optionally tighten the **Task page body** status lines if the loaded `/reflect` rules call for it

**Milestone Checkpoint:**
```
✓ REFLECTION CHECKPOINT
- Fix and scope reviewed? [YES/NO]
- Lessons / follow-ups captured? [YES/NO]
- Reflection artifact written? [YES/NO]

→ If all YES: Proceed to Archive
→ If any NO: Complete reflection steps
```

### Phase 4: ARCHIVE (`/archive`)

```mermaid
graph TD
    Start["Begin<br>Archive"] --> Record["Create Archive<br>completion record"]
    Record --> ActiveCtx["Remove this task’s<br>## Task … from Active Context"]
    ActiveCtx --> Handoff["Handoff /<br>next task ready"]
    Handoff --> ArchiveComplete["Archive<br>Complete"]
```

**Steps:**
1. Run **`/archive`** per loaded archive rules (Level 1 = minimal but complete closure)
2. Write the **Archive** subpage (`archivePageUrl`) when used; file-based: `memory-bank/archive/archive-[task_id].md`
3. **Mandatory (Notion):** remove the archived task’s **`## Task <taskId> — …`** block from **Active Context** (`activeContextPageUrl`); see **`Core/memory-bank-paths.mdc`**
4. Mark the task complete in your tracker / Task properties as required by those rules

**Milestone Checkpoint:**
```
✓ ARCHIVE CHECKPOINT
- Archive artifact created / updated? [YES/NO]
- Active Context cleaned for this task (Notion)? [YES/N/A]
- Task ready to close or switch? [YES/NO]

→ If all YES: Level 1 workflow complete
→ If any NO: Complete archive steps
```

## 📋 Task page body structure (Level 1)

For Level 1 tasks, use this minimal structure on the **Task page body** (Notion):

```markdown
## Bug Fixes in Progress
- [ ] [Level 1] Fix: [Bug description] (Est: XX mins)

## Completed Bug Fixes
- [X] [Level 1] Fixed: [Bug description] (Completed: YYYY-MM-DD)
  - Issue: [Brief issue description]
  - Solution: [Brief solution description]
  - Files changed: [File paths]
```

## 📋 MEMORY BANK UPDATES

For Level 1 tasks, make minimal Memory Bank updates:

1. **Task page body**: Update with fix details (through **/build** and touch-ups in **/reflect** if needed)
2. **Active Context** subpage (`activeContextPageUrl`): Brief mention during the task if relevant (merge-safe **`## Task …`** block); **/archive** removes that section when done
3. **Progress** subpage (`progressPageUrl`): Add to list of completed fixes
4. **Reflection** subpage (`reflectionPageUrl`): Brief structured reflection (**/reflect**)
5. **Archive** subpage (`archivePageUrl`) or equivalent: completion record (**/archive**)

## 📋 WORKFLOW VERIFICATION CHECKLIST

```
✓ FINAL WORKFLOW VERIFICATION
- Issue identified and understood? [YES/NO]
- Fix implemented and verified? [YES/NO]
- Task page body updated? [YES/NO]
- Reflection completed (Reflection subpage / file)? [YES/NO]
- Archive completed (Archive subpage / file; Active Context cleaned on Notion)? [YES/NO]
- Progress / minimal Memory Bank updates done? [YES/NO]

→ If all YES: Level 1 Task Successfully Completed
→ If any NO: Address outstanding items
```

## 📋 TASK ESCALATION

If during the Level 1 process you discover the task is more complex:

```
⚠️ TASK ESCALATION NEEDED
Current Level: Level 1
Recommended Level: Level [2/3/4]
Reason: [Brief explanation]

Would you like me to escalate this task to Level [2/3/4]?
```

Escalation indicators:
1. Fix requires changes to multiple components
2. Solution requires design decisions
3. Testing reveals broader issues
4. Fix impacts core functionality

